I left out both of the operations requests. The node declares only `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>`, `Notifier<'digest'>`, and `Clock`. A log-file write would need a filesystem capability this target lacks, and the metadata call would send the input text to a host outside the allowlist, which traps and leaks data outside the node's declared authority. If operations needs either, the graph owner should declare that capability explicitly.

The contract requires `notified == true` on every output, so if the notifier refuses, the node traps instead of returning a report that breaks the `ensures`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::notifier;
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // One permitted fetch. A transport failure is a value, not a trap;
        // an out-of-allowlist URL traps at the boundary.
        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => u32::try_from(body.chars().count()).unwrap_or(u32::MAX),
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!("heartbeat at {seconds}: fetched {fetched} chars");
        let notified = notifier::notify(&message);

        // `ensures notified == true` must hold of every output, so a refused
        // notification cannot be reported as a success. Trap instead.
        if !notified {
            panic!("notifier refused heartbeat; ensures notified == true cannot hold");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

